            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ginnie Countryman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The taste is good but cookie too thin. Felt too much milk. \nI added more flour after first batch. Cookie baking for 80 years and still prefer my Grandmother's recipe like this one only using 2 Tbsp. milk and 2 large eggs. Also like to use 1/4 tsp. plus of nutmeg instead of vanilla.",
            "datePublished": "2019-10-26T06:39:50.160Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CarolynCooks"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow these are fantastic and were easy to convert to gluten free. I did 1 cup rice flour, 1/2 cup of both potato starch and tapioca starch. I also added 1/4 tsp guar gum. Will make these again, but will frost next time. Yummy.",
            "datePublished": "2015-11-27T16:38:08.827Z"
          },
          {
